The '''2013 FA Community Shield''' (also known as '''The FA Community Shield sponsored by [[McDonald's]]''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 91st [[FA Community Shield]], played on 11 August 2013 at [[Wembley Stadium]], between the winners of the previous season's [[Premier League]] and [[FA Cup]] competitions. The match was contested by the champions of the [[2012–13 Premier League]], [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]], and the [[2012–13 FA Cup]] winners, [[Wigan Athletic F.C.|Wigan Athletic]].<ref>[http://www.thefa.com/News/competitions/fa-community-shield/2013/aug/manchester-united-wigan-athletic-wembley-twitter-updates.aspx United v Wigan]</ref> Following Wigan's relegation to the [[EFL Championship|Football League Championship]] just days after their cup triumph, it was the first time a team from outside the top flight had featured in the Community Shield since [[West Ham United F.C.|West Ham United]] in [[1980 FA Charity Shield|1980]].

[[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] were the holders, having won the [[2012 FA Community Shield|2012 edition]], but did not qualify for this match, as they finished second in the [[2012–13 Premier League|Premier League]] and lost the [[2013 FA Cup final|FA Cup final]].

Manchester United won the Shield for a record 16th time outright and 20th time overall after a 2–0 win over Wigan, with [[Robin van Persie]] scoring both goals. This season's Shield was notable for being [[David Moyes]]' only honour as Manchester United manager, in what was his first competitive match in charge of the club following the retirement of [[Alex Ferguson|Sir Alex Ferguson]] at the end of the 2012–13 season.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/news/0253-0d040800b931-9e725dc46575-1000--van-persie-double-earns-united-community-shield/|title = Van Persie double earns United Community Shield|date = 11 August 2013|publisher=UEFA}}</ref>

